{
 "@context": {
  "dcterms": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
  "owl": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#",
  "prov": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#",
  "rdf": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#",
  "rdfs": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#",
  "schema": "https://schema.org/",
  "skos": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#",
  "wd": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/",
  "wg": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/",
  "wgo": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#",
  "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
 },
 "@graph": [
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I considered how this problem looks across the person's whole life, past and future, and not only today?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I named what I do not know about this situation, and what I would do if things turn out differently than I expect?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging this choice by my own values only, or have I tried to understand the values and priorities behind it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:berlin-wisdom-paradigm"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I wishing this person well, or am I telling myself that what they did was fine?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this wrong still going on and within my power to change, so that action rather than reappraisal is the priority?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After the exercise, what concrete step, if any, does fairness to me or others still require?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I trying this because I'm ready, or because I feel I ought to have moved on by now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:compassionate-reappraisal"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "They were wrong to blame me, and I'll correct the record with the manager tomorrow. They were scared of being blamed, which doesn't excuse it, and I hope they learn to own their mistakes. I can wish them that and still watch my back.",
   "wgo:before": "I keep going over every word they said to the manager. They're two-faced, that's all there is to it, and I'll be cold to them from now on.",
   "wgo:situation": "A teammate missed a handover deadline and then told your manager the delay was your fault, and you lie awake replaying it.",
   "wgo:why": "Replaying the offence keeps anger and arousal high, while seeing the person as flawed and in need of change lets the anger ease without denying the wrong or giving up the practical response."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Compassionate reappraisal",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Sit somewhere quiet and settle your breathing for a minute or two before you start."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Recall one specific time a particular person hurt or wronged you, and name plainly what they did and what it cost you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Picture the offender as a whole person with a history, fears and other sides to them, not only as the author of this act."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Treat the wrong as a sign that this person needs to grow or change, without telling yourself it was acceptable."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Try, for about two minutes, to sincerely wish them something good, such as healing or becoming someone who would not do this again."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Notice your thoughts, feelings and body as you do this, and repeat the exercise when you catch yourself replaying the hurt."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Decide separately, on the facts, what boundary, conversation or accountability the situation still needs."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this decision actually within my power, and is the outcome really uncertain, or am I deliberating to put off accepting something?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I checked that the goal itself is a good one, not just how to reach it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I consider more than one way forward before settling on the first idea I had?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my confidence here earned by long, well-fed-back experience, or is it just a strong feeling?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I set a point where thinking stops and acting starts?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:deliberation"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Is this really my call, and what am I trying to achieve: her success, or a quieter team? Let me list the options, including a coaching plan with a review date, talk it over with HR and her previous lead, and decide by Thursday.",
   "wgo:before": "My gut says she's not cut out for this. I'll announce the move on Monday and be done with it.",
   "wgo:situation": "A manager has to decide within a week whether to move a struggling analyst to a different team or keep coaching her in her current role.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response clarifies the goal, widens the options and borrows others' judgment on an important, uncertain matter, but still commits to a decision on time instead of drifting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Deliberation",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Check that the matter is actually up to you and that its outcome is genuinely uncertain; if not, stop deliberating and either accept it or act on what is known."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Say plainly what you are trying to achieve, and ask whether that end is worth pursuing before you plan how to reach it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "List at least two or three realistic ways of getting there, not just the first one that occurred to you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "For the most promising option, trace backwards from the goal to the very next thing you would have to do, and drop options whose chain hits something impossible."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "If the decision is important, talk it through with someone who knows this kind of situation."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Before trusting a strong gut feeling, ask whether you have had long, well-fed-back experience with situations like this one."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Set a point at which deliberation ends, then choose and act promptly, without reopening the question unless new facts appear."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which way do I usually err in situations like this one, too much or too little, and am I correcting for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I calling a choice \"balanced\" just because it sits halfway between two options, rather than because it fits the situation?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the strength of my reaction proportionate to how serious this actually is?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:doctrine-of-the-mean"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/doctrine-of-the-mean/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I tend to avoid conflict, so I'll lean a little firmer than feels natural: a private conversation, the specific facts, what I need by when, and a real question about what is getting in his way.",
   "wgo:before": "Either I let it slide to keep the peace, or I lay it all out bluntly in front of the team so nobody can say I'm soft.",
   "wgo:situation": "A newly promoted team lead has to tell a long-serving colleague that his reports keep arriving late and incomplete.",
   "wgo:why": "The right degree of firmness depends on this person and this problem, and knowing which way you usually err tells you which way to correct, as Aristotle advised."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I actually tried to understand how this looks from their side, or am I assuming I already know?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I feeling with them, or am I now caught up in my own distress about their distress?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my empathy here going only to the person who is closest, most like me or most vivid, while others affected stay invisible?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After understanding what they feel, what would actually help them, as opposed to what would relieve my discomfort?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:empathy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I take a minute to really listen and say it back: 'Months of work, and it's gone. That's a real loss.' I notice the heaviness in me, remind myself it is their loss, not mine, and ask what would help. Later I check in and offer a concrete hand with the next project.",
   "wgo:before": "I absorb their upset so fully that I feel sick about it too, then I either pile on about how unfair management is or quietly avoid them for the rest of the week because it is too much.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague tells you, close to tears, that their project has been cancelled after months of work, and you have your own deadline in an hour.",
   "wgo:why": "Feeling with someone opens the door, but staying clear about whose feeling it is and turning it into warm concern and practical help keeps you from either drowning in their distress or backing away from it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reacting to what actually happened, or to the story I am telling about it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my calm here steadiness, or am I simply refusing to feel or to care?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If this turned out well, or badly, would I still be able to act on my values?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What part of this is up to me, and am I putting my energy there?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:equanimity"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "That hurts, and I'll let myself feel it. What's in my hands now is an honest account of what we learned and what we'll try differently, so that's what I'll present.",
   "wgo:before": "This is a disaster. I'll open with who dropped the ball, and frankly I'm not sure this team can win anything.",
   "wgo:situation": "An hour before you present to leadership, you learn that the client your team spent three months courting has chosen a competitor.",
   "wgo:why": "The loss is still felt, but it no longer chooses your words; attention moves from blame and panic to the part of the situation you can actually shape."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I holding on to this to protect myself or someone else, or mainly to make them pay?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I separated forgiving from excusing, forgetting and reconciling, so I know which of these I'm actually being asked to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If they keep doing this, what boundary would self-respect require alongside any forgiveness?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I given myself time to name the hurt before deciding whether, and how, to forgive?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:forgiveness"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/forgiveness/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll tell them plainly that it was wrong and that I'll put my name on my own work from now on. Then I'll stop rehearsing it and treat them fairly on this project.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll be polite, but I'm keeping score, and I'll make sure the client finds out what they're really like.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague presented your analysis as their own to a client, later admitted it and apologised, and you still have to work together on the account.",
   "wgo:why": "Forgiving here means dropping the campaign of payback while keeping the judgement that it was wrong and the safeguards that protect you; it is neither pretending nothing happened nor trusting blindly."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I noticed who made this good thing possible, and the effort or intention it took them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I actually told them, specifically, rather than only feeling it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my thanks free, or am I acting out of a sense of debt, guilt or deference I don't really owe?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using \"be grateful\" to talk myself, or someone else, out of a legitimate complaint?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:gratitude"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll tell them specifically what their evening saved, mention it to our manager, and keep an eye out for a chance to help them in turn.",
   "wgo:before": "Good, it's fixed. That's their job anyway; on to the next thing.",
   "wgo:situation": "A teammate quietly stayed late to fix a broken data feed so your quarterly report could go out on time.",
   "wgo:why": "Gratitude notices both the benefit and the goodwill behind it, then answers with thanks and goodwill rather than taking it for granted or treating it as a debt to settle and forget."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If the other person later learned everything I know, would they feel I had misled them, even if every word I said was true?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I keeping quiet here out of tact, or out of fear of an awkward moment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is the kind thing I am about to say also accurate, and is the accurate thing I am about to say also kind?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What am I telling myself about my own part in this that I would not want someone else to check?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:honesty"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Not for Friday, as things stand. We found a data issue yesterday. I'll have a revised date and options to you by this afternoon.",
   "wgo:before": "We're in good shape. There are a few loose ends, but nothing to worry about.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your manager asks, in front of the team, whether the migration you lead is on track for Friday. It is not; a data problem surfaced yesterday and you have not yet told anyone.",
   "wgo:why": "The first answer contains no outright lie but is built to mislead, and it spends trust the team will need when the slip comes out. The second states the fact plainly, owns the delay, and pairs bad news with a next step."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I dismissing this objection because of its evidence, or because of who raised it and how well things have gone for me lately?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When did someone last change my mind on something important, and did I make it easy or costly for them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who, if anyone, can still stop me from making this decision, and have I given them what they need to do so?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating my organisation's success as proof of my own judgment?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:hubris"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"My recent wins are a reason to check myself, not to skip the check. Walk me through your demand figures, and let's have finance stress-test both versions before the board sees either.\" The plan is approved a quarter later at a smaller scale, with a review point.",
   "wgo:before": "\"I've called it right every time so far, and the numbers will catch up with the vision. We're not slowing down for a spreadsheet.\" The analyst stops raising concerns, and the plan goes ahead unchanged.",
   "wgo:situation": "A department head has delivered three strong years in a row and been praised in the trade press. A senior analyst warns that a proposed expansion rests on optimistic demand figures.",
   "wgo:why": "Recent success and praise are exactly the conditions under which leaders overpay and overreach; deliberately inviting the dissenting case and an independent check restores the feedback that power tends to cut off."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When did I last tell my team, in so many words, that I was wrong about something?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Who did the real work on this result, and have the people above me heard their names?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking for input because I will use it, or to look open?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Does this situation call for listening and learning, or for a fast, clear decision that I can review with the team later?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:humble-leadership"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I under-estimated testing, and Priya flagged it in March; I should have listened. Here's the revised plan. Priya, can you walk me through how you sized it so I get it right next time?",
   "wgo:before": "The vendors let us down and testing turned out harder than anyone could have predicted. We'll push harder.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project lead's schedule for a product launch slips by three weeks, partly because she under-estimated the testing work, and an analyst on the team had flagged the risk early.",
   "wgo:why": "Owning the error, crediting the person who saw it and asking to learn from her makes it safe for others to raise risks early, and it fixes the estimating method rather than just the date."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Humble leadership",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "When you get something wrong or don't know the answer, say so plainly and early, and say what you will do about it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Name specific contributions by specific people, in their hearing and when reporting upward; say \"we\" for shared wins and \"I\" for your own errors."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Ask the team for feedback on one concrete thing you did, listen without defending, and tell them later what you changed."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Let people with more expertise on a task teach you, in front of others if possible."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Keep making clear decisions; in a crisis or under tight deadlines, act first and invite reflection afterwards."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/humble-leadership/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Check that the humility is believed, not read as a tactic, by keeping your private conduct consistent with what you say in meetings."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I call someone wise, am I responding to their judgment and care for others, or mainly to their intelligence, confidence or age?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Whose advice am I about to rely on here, and what picture of wisdom made me choose them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would someone raised with a different idea of wisdom see this choice as wise, and what would they weigh that I am leaving out?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:implicit-theories-of-wisdom"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of my view have I actually checked, and which part am I only sure of?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What evidence or argument would change my mind here, and have I gone looking for it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When I was shown a mistake just now, did I feel curiosity or did I feel attacked?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I underselling a strength I really do have, out of false modesty or fear of conflict?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:intellectual-humility"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "You're right, I didn't test that assumption. Let's rerun it with your figure and see how much the forecast moves. Thanks for catching it.",
   "wgo:before": "The model is fine. The market just shifted; nobody could have seen that coming.",
   "wgo:situation": "In a project review, a colleague points out that the sales forecast you built last month rests on an assumption you never checked.",
   "wgo:why": "Owning the gap, rather than blaming circumstances or brushing it off, fixes the forecast, shows the team that errors can be raised safely, and treats the critic as an ally in getting it right."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would someone who knows me well say about me here that I would rather not hear?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I judging myself by my intentions while others can only see my behaviour?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I mistaken a confident story about my motives for real knowledge of them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:know-thyself"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I don't experience myself that way, but two people saw the same thing. I'll ask a colleague to watch the next meeting and tell me what they notice.",
   "wgo:before": "That's not me. I know how I come across, and I'm a good listener.",
   "wgo:situation": "After a project review, a manager is told by two team members that her meetings run long because she rarely lets others finish a point.",
   "wgo:why": "Self-views are least reliable on flattering or unflattering traits, so treating others' observations as evidence rather than an attack is how the maxim is actually followed."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking what I want from life, or what this situation is asking of me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there anything left for me to create, experience or stand for here, even if the outcome is out of my hands?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I watching myself so closely that it is getting in the way of what I'm trying to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:logotherapy"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The project is gone, but the people I trained and what we learned stay. What do I want to build next, and how do I want to carry this?",
   "wgo:before": "None of it mattered. I'll keep my head down and stop caring about the work.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team's long-running project is cancelled after a reorganisation, and a project lead feels the past year was wasted.",
   "wgo:why": "Looking for meaning in contribution, relationships and chosen attitude, rather than only in outcomes you control, keeps a setback from emptying out the whole effort."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Logotherapy",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name one thing you are creating or contributing right now, however small, and who it serves."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Name one experience or person you value that you could give more attention to this week."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For a hardship you cannot change, decide what stance toward it you want to be able to look back on."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Turn your attention from monitoring yourself to the task or person in front of you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating \"not deciding\" as if it were not itself a choice?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I assuming the person I'll be in ten years wants exactly what I want today?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of this can I learn about before committing, and which part can I only learn by living it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:major-life-decision"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I can't know now what teaching will feel like, and staying is a choice too. I'll test what I can (shadow a class, ask two teachers what surprised them), decide what I'd want to have tried, and set a date.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll wait until I'm sure I'll be happier as a teacher. Until then, staying put is the safe choice.",
   "wgo:situation": "After eight years in a stable accounting job, Priya has an offer to retrain as a teacher at lower pay, and has been going back and forth for months.",
   "wgo:why": "Waiting for a certainty that can't arrive quietly chooses the status quo, which the evidence suggests people over-favour; gathering what is knowable and naming the real reasons is the wiser path."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If my time were shorter than I assume, would this still be worth my anger or effort?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the thought of death to clarify what matters, or to feed dread or reckless indulgence?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would I want to have said or done for the people involved here?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:memento-mori"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "If my time were shorter than I assume, this exchange would not be worth another evening. I'll send a short, civil reply tomorrow and spend tonight with the people in the next room.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll send a reply that puts them in their place, then keep going through my inbox until midnight.",
   "wgo:situation": "You have spent a week stewing over a curt email from a colleague and are drafting a sharp reply late in the evening while your family is in the next room.",
   "wgo:why": "Remembering that time is limited and uncertain shifts attention from winning a minor status contest to the relationships and values you would actually want to have served."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Memento mori",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Pick a fixed cue for the reflection, such as waking up, a commute, or the last few minutes before sleep."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Bring to mind, concretely and in your own case, that your life will end and that you do not know when."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Look back over the last day or week and ask how you actually spent your time and attention."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask what you would regret leaving undone or unsaid, and whom you would think of first."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Choose one concrete action for today that reflects what matters, and let go of one petty grievance or craving."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/memento-mori/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Return your attention to the task in front of you; if the reflection leaves you more anxious than clear, shorten it or stop."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I collect reasons over a few days, or only those that occurred to me in one mood?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I weigh the reasons, or just count which column was longer?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there one reason so important that it should settle this on its own, whatever the rest of the list says?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the list to choose, or to talk myself out of something I had already decided to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Now that the balance is clear, have I set a time to act on it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:moral-algebra"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll keep a Pro and Con page on my phone for the next four days, weigh the reasons on Friday, and see what's left after cancelling the equal ones. If the only big thing on the Con side is my partner's job, that's a conversation to have before I answer, not a line to cancel out.",
   "wgo:before": "It sounds exciting and I hate saying no to leadership. I'll accept in tomorrow's one-to-one and sort out the details later.",
   "wgo:situation": "A project manager is offered a two-year posting to the company's office in another city and has to reply within a week.",
   "wgo:why": "Gathering reasons over several days stops the mood of one meeting from deciding, weighing rather than counting keeps a single heavy reason from being outvoted by trivia, and the final check surfaces the reason that really matters."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Moral algebra",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Use the method only for an important choice that is up to you and genuinely two-sided, not for a matter of taste or a change you have already committed to."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Frame one specific option (for example, \"accept the transfer\") and divide a page into two columns headed Pro and Con."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Over three or four days, add a short note to either column whenever a reason occurs to you, instead of trying to list everything in one sitting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Bring all the reasons into view and give each a rough weight, such as 1 to 3."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Strike out pairs of reasons of equal weight on opposite sides, and let one strong reason cancel two or three weaker ones that together equal it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Ask whether any single remaining reason is decisive on its own, or whether a reason you never wrote down is the one actually driving you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Wait a day or two; if no important new reason appears, decide by the balance and act on it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I rehearsing a possible loss in order to prepare and appreciate, or am I just worrying?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "After imagining this loss, did I come back to what I still have and what I can do now?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which parts of the outcome I fear are actually up to me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:negative-visualization"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Once, I'll list what could go wrong in the presentation, prepare for the questions I can foresee, and accept that the reaction isn't fully up to me. And I'll take a minute to picture not having this job at all, then notice what I'd miss.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll keep replaying how badly the presentation could go every night until then, and keep grumbling about this job.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your manager asks you to present to senior leadership next week, and you also have a job you mostly enjoy but have started to complain about.",
   "wgo:why": "A brief, bounded rehearsal turns vague fear into preparation and restores appreciation, whereas dwelling on the worst only adds suffering before anything has happened."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Negative visualization",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Choose one thing you value and tend to take for granted, such as a relationship, your health, your job or an ordinary comfort."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Remind yourself plainly of its nature, starting small, for example that this mug can break and that the people you love are mortal."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "For a minute or two, imagine concretely what your life would be like without it, or how it might never have come about."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Return to the present and notice that you do still have it; name one way you will use or appreciate it today."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Before a risky plan, list what could go wrong, separate what is up to you from what is not, and prepare for the parts you can influence."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Stop if the exercise turns into dread or repetitive worry, and shorten it or set it aside."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I imagining how they feel, or how I would feel in their place?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which of my beliefs about their view have I actually checked with them?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I asked a question I don't already know the answer to?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there an option that meets what they want as well as what I want?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:perspective-taking"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I sketch what their fortnight probably looked like, note that I'm guessing, then ask privately how the project is going from their side. It turns out a second project landed on them without my knowing; we reprioritise together.",
   "wgo:before": "I decide they've stopped caring, picture how I'd feel if I were slacking, and send a sharp message about accountability.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead notices that a usually reliable colleague has missed two deadlines in a row and seems curt in meetings.",
   "wgo:why": "Imagining their side softened my reaction, but only asking told me what was actually going on; taking and getting perspective together led to a fair and workable fix."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Perspective-taking",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before you respond, name your own first reading of the situation so you can set it aside for a moment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Imagine the other person's day, constraints and goals, and ask what they know that you don't and what they want from this."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Write down two or three guesses about how they see it, and mark each one as a guess."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Check the guesses by asking open questions (\"How does this look from where you sit?\") and listen without rebutting."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Revise your reading with what you heard, then decide what to do, looking for an option that serves both of you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there still something I can do about this, or is it time to let the goal go and invest in another?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I learning a specific lesson from this regret, or replaying the same scene and blaming myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I speak to a friend with this regret the way I am speaking to myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which choice in front of me now am I most likely to regret not making?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:regret"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/regret/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I did hold back, and I wish I hadn't. What was I afraid of, and is that still true? The next lead role opens in spring, so this month I'll ask my manager for a stretch project and say plainly that I want to be considered.",
   "wgo:before": "I always bottle it. I keep replaying that week and telling myself what an idiot I was, or I insist I have no regrets at all and change the subject.",
   "wgo:situation": "Two years ago you decided not to apply for a team-lead role; a colleague got it and is thriving, and the news of their promotion brings the old decision back.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response accepts the regret without self-attack, extracts the lesson and turns it toward an opportunity that is still open, which is when regret is most useful."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is what I am about to say true, as far as I actually know, or is it a guess or a convenient story?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Will saying it help them or the situation, or does it mainly serve my comfort, my image or my wish to be right?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this the right moment and the right tone for them to be able to hear it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I holding back something true and useful only because saying it would be awkward for me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did anything I said today divide people, wound someone needlessly or pass on gossip, and is there something I should put right?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:right-speech"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "The analysis is strong. One thing to fix before tomorrow: slide 6 uses last quarter's cost assumption, which finance dropped. Want ten minutes in the morning to swap in the new number? Everything else I'd leave as it is.",
   "wgo:before": "\"Looks great, you'll be fine!\" Or, at 11 pm, a long message listing every weakness you can find, ending with a suggestion to rethink the whole thing.",
   "wgo:situation": "The evening before a colleague presents to senior leadership, they send you their slides and ask, \"Is this ready?\" The analysis is solid, but the cost figure on slide 6 rests on an assumption you know finance has already rejected.",
   "wgo:why": "The first reply is pleasing but untrue and leaves them exposed; the second is true but harsh, badly timed and more about your critique than their success. The wiser reply is true, useful and timed so it can be acted on, and its goodwill is plain."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Right speech",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Before saying anything that matters, ask first whether it is true as far as you actually know, and drop it if it is not, however pleasing it would be."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask next whether it is beneficial, meaning it will help the listener or the situation rather than only relieve your feelings or win the point."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "If it is true and beneficial but unwelcome, do not swallow it; choose a time when the person can hear it, and plan to say it plainly and gently."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Check your motive and tone, and speak from goodwill rather than irritation, contempt or a wish to look good."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "While you are speaking, notice whether the words are causing needless hurt, and stop, slow down or rephrase if they are."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Afterwards, review the conversation; if your words did harm, admit it to the person or a trusted friend and resolve to do better, and if they went well, note what helped."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/right-speech/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Watch for the four habits the tradition names, lying, divisive talebearing, harsh words and idle chatter, especially in casual talk where they are easiest to miss."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Has this round of thinking produced a new insight or a next step, or am I replaying the same scene?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I asking how to deal with this, or only why it happened and what it says about me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What would I advise a friend in exactly this position, and can I take that advice tonight?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I tested the fear I keep circling, or only rehearsed it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:rumination"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/rumination/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "\"If a colleague told me this, I'd ask what exactly went wrong and what they'd do next. The last three updates slipped because I waited for complete data. I'll propose a short interim update every Friday and check that works for her.\" Then you put it down for the night.",
   "wgo:before": "\"Why do I always do this? What does she really think of me? I'm probably the weakest person on the team.\" Two hours later you are still replaying the meeting and have decided nothing.",
   "wgo:situation": "In your annual review, your manager says your project updates are often late. That night you cannot stop thinking about it.",
   "wgo:why": "Asking what happened and how to act, from a step back, turns the same worry into a plan, whereas asking why in a self-critical loop keeps the hurt fresh and leaves the problem untouched."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/adversity-and-mortality",
