  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/wisdom-traditions",
   "@type": "skos:ConceptScheme",
   "skos:prefLabel": "Wisdom traditions"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I ask people who know this kind of decision, or only people who would agree with me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:seeking-counsel"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Did I ask without signalling the answer I wanted?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:seeking-counsel"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "When the advice differed from my view, did I actually move, or did I explain it away?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:seeking-counsel"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I asked anyone who has already lived through this choice how it felt afterwards?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:seeking-counsel"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I'll write down my own answer first, then ask a former colleague who joined a start-up two years ago how it really went, and a mentor who tends to be cautious. I won't tell them which way I'm leaning, and I'll actually shift my view if they both raise the same worry.",
   "wgo:before": "I'll ask my best friend, who always backs me, mention the salary first, and take the yes as confirmation.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead has a job offer from a fast-growing start-up and must answer by Friday. They are excited and have already half-decided to accept.",
   "wgo:why": "Asking advisers who know the terrain, without steering them, gives the decision a second independent view and the lived experience of someone who has already been there, which people tend to undervalue."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Seeking counsel",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the decision and decide whether it is important and uncertain enough to deserve outside counsel."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Write down your own current view and how confident you are, before you ask anyone."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Choose two or three advisers who know this kind of situation, including at least one who has lived through it and one likely to disagree with you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask each one separately and personally, describe the problem without revealing your preferred answer, and ask what they would do and why."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Ask anyone who has already been through the same choice how it actually turned out and felt for them."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Compare their answers with your own and move your view meaningfully toward the advice where they know more or agree with each other, noting where and why you still differ."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Make the decision yourself, take responsibility for it, and later tell your advisers what you decided and how it went."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I reliving this from the inside, or looking at it as an observer would?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:self-distancing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I give a friend in my position the advice I am about to follow?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:self-distancing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I asked what I might not know and how the other person sees this?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:self-distancing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is this distance helping me understand the feeling, or helping me avoid it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:self-distancing"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Why is Jordan so rattled by one line? Jordan doesn't yet know what the manager meant by 'the point'. If a friend showed me this, I'd tell them to ask one clarifying question on Monday, not to send a reply at midnight.",
   "wgo:before": "I can't believe I got this so wrong. I'll keep rereading that comment, write a defensive reply tonight and hit send.",
   "wgo:situation": "Late on a Friday, your manager leaves a blunt comment on your project report saying the analysis \"misses the point\", and you feel your weekend souring.",
   "wgo:why": "Viewing the moment as an observer cools the sting enough to admit what you don't know and to consider the other person's view, which is the kind of reasoning people find easier about a friend's problem than their own."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Self-distancing",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Notice the signs that you are immersed in an upsetting experience, such as replaying the same scene, rehearsing the same sentence or feeling the original anger or shame rise again."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Shift your vantage point by picturing the scene from across the room, as a neutral observer would see it, with yourself as one of the people in it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Talk to yourself silently using your own name or \"you\" instead of \"I\", for example \"Why is Sam so stung by this?\""
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Ask what lies behind the feeling and what you might be missing, rather than recounting again what happened."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Widen the frame by asking how the other people involved might see it, and how the situation could change over the coming months."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Ask what you would advise a friend in exactly this position, then choose one concrete next step."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Stop if the distance is turning into a way of avoiding the feeling or the problem, and seek support if the distress persists."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Do I actually know this, or am I only confident about it?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:socratic-ignorance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If someone questioned me closely here, where would my account run out?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:socratic-ignorance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating skill in my own field as if it made me an authority on this question too?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:socratic-ignorance"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I've only skimmed it, so I don't actually know. Here's what I'd need to check, and who has worked with them before?",
   "wgo:before": "Yes, they're solid, I'm sure of it. Let's lock them in.",
   "wgo:situation": "A team lead is asked in a planning meeting whether a new supplier can deliver on time, and has only skimmed their proposal.",
   "wgo:why": "Separating what you know from what you merely feel sure of keeps a confident guess from becoming the team's decision, and invites the people who do know to speak."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "If a friend brought me this exact problem, what would I tell them, and am I following that advice myself?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:solomons-paradox"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Could I state the other person's view in words they would accept as fair?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:solomons-paradox"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I admitted what I don't know about their motives and about how this could unfold?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:solomons-paradox"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I treating any compromise as a defeat?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:solomons-paradox"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "If my teammate described this to me, I'd ask what they actually know about the peer's reasons, what a fair split could look like, and how it might look in a month. I'll ask the peer for ten minutes first.",
   "wgo:before": "This is a power grab, plain and simple. I know exactly what they're up to, and I'm escalating to our director today.",
   "wgo:situation": "You recently helped a teammate think calmly through a clash with another department. This week a peer quietly reassigns part of your own project without asking you.",
   "wgo:why": "Treating your own conflict as you would a colleague's brings back the habits you already use as an adviser, namely admitting what you don't know, looking for compromise and expecting the situation to change."
  },
