  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I trying to understand what is really going on here, including what I cannot know, or only looking for facts that confirm my first reaction?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Have I looked at this situation, and my own part in it, from at least one other person's point of view?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is my response moved by concern for the people affected, or mainly by protecting my ego?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:three-dimensional-wisdom-model"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Seen from far above and years from now, how big is this, really?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Am I using the wider view to act better here, or to stop caring about people who are affected?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Which part of this is about my reputation, and which part is about what is right to do?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:view-from-above"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "Picture this from far above: one meeting among millions happening today, which few will remember next year. What matters is the project and how I treat people. I'll sleep on it, then ask my manager what would have made my proposal stronger.",
   "wgo:before": "Everyone saw that. I'm sending this tonight so they know the decision was wrong and I won't be pushed aside.",
   "wgo:situation": "A colleague's proposal is chosen over yours in front of the whole department, and you spend the evening composing a sharp reply-all email.",
   "wgo:why": "Seeing the slight at its real scale lowers the heat of the moment, and coming back down to one useful action keeps the wider view from turning into either revenge or indifference."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "The view from above",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/6"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Name the specific thing that is gripping you right now, such as a slight, a setback, a rivalry or a wish for praise."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Picture yourself rising slowly above the room, the building and the city until you can see whole countries and the many lives going on in them at once."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Widen the view in time as well, recalling the people who lived before you and those who will come after, few of whom will ever know of this moment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "From that height, look back at your situation and ask how large it really is, and what part of it actually depends on you."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Come back down deliberately and choose one concrete, decent action for today, so the wider view ends in conduct rather than detachment."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/view-from-above/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Stop and set the exercise aside if it leaves you feeling that nothing matters, and talk to someone you trust instead."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/1",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "What don't I know about this situation, and how sure am I really about the other person's motives?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/2",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Could I describe the other side's view in words they would accept as fair?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/3",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "How might this look in a month or a year, and what else could happen besides the outcome I fear?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/4",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Is there an arrangement that meets the main concerns on both sides, or am I treating any middle ground as losing?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/check/5",
   "@type": "wgo:SelfCheckQuestion",
   "rdfs:label": "Would I reason about this differently if a friend had brought it to me?",
   "wgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "wg:wise-reasoning"
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning/example",
   "@type": "wgo:Rewrite",
   "wgo:after": "I don't yet know why this was decided or who pushed for it. I'll ask the lead what problem the merger solves, say plainly what I think would be lost, and propose a handover that keeps the parts that work. This may look different in three months.",
   "wgo:before": "They have clearly sidelined me on purpose. I'll tell the team the plan is a mistake and refuse to hand anything over.",
   "wgo:situation": "Your team lead announces that a project you have run for a year will be merged into another group's work. You learn about it in the same meeting as everyone else.",
   "wgo:why": "The wiser response admits what it does not know, takes the other side's reasons seriously, allows that events can still turn several ways, and looks for an arrangement both sides can live with, which are the four elements researchers score."
  },
