   },
   "skos:definition": "The character trait of reliably not distorting the facts as you understand them, whether by lying, misleading, cheating, stealing or breaking promises, out of care for truth and for the people who depend on it rather than out of fear of being caught; practised wisely, it is joined to tact, timing and kindness rather than to bluntness.",
