   ],
   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "wg:self-knowledge"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The ancient Greek maxim inscribed at Apollo's temple at Delphi, read first as a reminder of human limits and later, through Socrates and Plato, as a call to examine one's own character, beliefs and ignorance; modern psychology adds that this is best done with the help of other people's views.",
